{"mathCache":"","mathFallback":false,"description":"JEE Main's 2021 JEE Main 2021 (Online) 26th February Morning Shift Paper's All Questions with solutions provider ExamSIDE.Com","paperTitle":"JEE Main 2021 (Online) 26th February Morning Shift","nextq":"wrvo2JTJ5c8kR6aM7R1kludnpno","prevq":"2wKz6rJGqBZP9jufpP1kluc60hc","questions":[{"question_id":"yTKueDaZTjGERgKmFP1klucw2q7","chapter":"basics-of-organic-chemistry","chapterGroup":"organic-chemistry","country":"in","difficulty":"easy","exam":"jee-main","examGroup":"jee","languages":["en"],"marks":4,"negMarks":1,"paperTitle":"JEE Main 2021 (Online) 26th February Morning Shift","permalink":"given-below-are-two-statements-brbrstatement-i--a-mi-jee-main-chemistry-some-basic-concepts-of-chemistry-o1tdv1olbtfxhaen","question":{"en":{"direction":null,"content":"Given below are two statements :<br><br>Statement I : A mixture of chloroform and aniline can be separated by simple distillation.<br><br>Statement II : When separating aniline from a mixture of aniline and water by steam distillation aniline boils below its boiling point.<br><br>In the light of the above statements, choose the most appropriate answer from the options given below :","options":[{"identifier":"A","content":"Both Statement I and Statement II are true"},{"identifier":"B","content":"Both Statement I and Statement II are false"},{"identifier":"C","content":"Statement I is true but Statement II is false"},{"identifier":"D","content":"Statement I is false but Statement II is true"}],"correct_options":["A"],"answer":null,"explanation":"Mixture of chloroform and aniline can be\nseparated by simple distillation as these\ntwo liquids have sufficient difference in\nboiling point.\nChloroform (b.p. 334 K), aniline (b.p. 457 K)\n<br><br> In steam distillation, if one of the\nsubstances is water and the other, a water\ninsoluble substance (like aniline) then the\nmixture will boil close to but below 373 K."},"hi":{"direction":null,"content":"नीचे दिए गए हैं दो कथन :